{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And you I will scatter, etc.</b> The verse may be explained along the lines of what Amram, of blessed memory, [stated] in tractate Ketubot (111a): that HaShem adjured Israel with three oaths — one, that they not storm the wall, meaning by force of arms; and one, that they not rebel against the nations of the world, etc. — so far [is the Gemara's language]. And this is the meaning of <b>And you I will scatter among the nations</b>: here He alluded to two things. His saying <b>I will scatter</b> alludes to [the oath] that they not storm the wall; <b>among the nations</b> alludes to [the oath] that they not rebel against the nations. And His saying <b>and I will draw out a sword after you</b> may be explained along the lines of what the Gemara concludes there, and this is its language: The Holy One, blessed be He, said to Israel: If you fulfill the oath — well and good; and if not, I will permit your flesh [to be hunted] like the gazelles and the deer of the field — so far [is the Gemara's language]. And this is His saying <b>and I will draw out a sword after you</b>: that a drawn sword will be before you, if you do not fulfill the decree of scattering among the nations — as mentioned, your flesh will be [given over], etc. Furthermore, His saying <b>and your land shall be</b> a desolation — this gives the reason for the matter: why does HaShem desire the scattering among the nations? So that the land be a desolation and the cities in ruins, for then the land will desire [its children to return], etc. For this reason it is necessary that you be in the land of your enemies, and this is what it says: ״And you״ etc."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:02:30.061355577Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}